{0 Gamelle}

Gamelle is a tiny 2D game engine. It provides:

- Hot code reload on every file change for a quick feedback loop
- Export to a single HTML file to share your game online
- Automatic assets loading for images, sounds and fonts
- Immediate mode GUI to quickly put together menus and widgets
- Collisions detection and rigid physics

{1 API}

- {!module-Gamelle} — the game engine: main loop, drawing, inputs, UI,
  physics, networking.
- {!module-Gamelle_physics} — the backend-free core (geometry and rigid-body
  physics), for headless programs such as game servers.

{1 Examples}

Playable in the browser, compiled with [js_of_ocaml]; the source code lives in
the {{:https://github.com/art-w/gamelle/tree/master/examples}[examples/]}
directory of the repository.

- {{:../examples/volley.html}Volley} — volleyball with rigid physics, two
  players on one keyboard
- {{:../examples/volley_multi.html}Volley multi} — the same game with menus
  and online multiplayer: create or join a game by its 5-digit code (requires
  a running volley-server)
- {{:../examples/pong.html}Pong}
- {{:../examples/snake.html}Snake}
- {{:../examples/morpion.html}Morpion} — tic-tac-toe
- {{:../examples/trigonometry_sprint.html}Trigonometry sprint}
- {{:../examples/sound.html}Sound} — sound and music playback
- {{:../examples/ui.html}Ui} — tour of the immediate mode GUI widgets
- {{:../examples/routine.html}Routine} — time-based animation combinators


{1 Getting started}

You can create a new game project with:

{@shell[
  $ gamelle init mygame
  $ cd mygame
  $ make
]}

The [make] command starts the game in development mode: editing
[src/mygame.ml] will automatically reload your game on every change. Game
assets added to the folder [assets/] are automatically available through the
dynamic [Assets] module.

To export your game as a single HTML file, compiled with [js_of_ocaml] and
including all game assets:

{@shell[
  $ make html
]}
